WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.250
[ MUSIC PLAYING ] 

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:13.042
It feels like somebody's, like,
squeezing your heart.

00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:15.459
That's how I felt.
Very gut-wrenching.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:18.834
Just be prepared for lots--
lots of emotions.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.417
The idea of shooting this film

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:27.542
came about in the beginning
of 2018.

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:29.834
We were all just kinda taking
a leap of faith.

00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:33.209
We were all pretty, um,
what's the word?

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.417
skeptical I think
is the word.

00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:37.000
I just didn't ever think
it was going to happen.

00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:38.709
I was like, "Oh, yeah,
they're going to film me.

00:00:38.751 --> 00:00:41.000
But, eh, they're not going
to make a movie, you know?

00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:42.584
They're just gonna film
a bunch of ( bleep )

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:44.501
and they're never going
to actually make a doc.

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:46.959
Never going to actually, like,
put it out there in the world.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.792
We're never going to see it."
But they did.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:51.042
And they made a good one.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:58.083
Really ( bleep ) emotional.

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:00.918
Oh, my God.
Let me start over.

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:03.250
When we first watched it,

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:05.417
we were in my living room.

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.209
I knew there was
some stuff in there

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.542
that I was going to be
mortified by.

00:01:09.584 --> 00:01:13.542
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:13.584 --> 00:01:15.542
( bleep ) happened, so...

00:01:15.584 --> 00:01:18.417
But I cried out of joy
for a lot of it

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:21.000
because I guess I didn't really
put together the fact

00:01:21.042 --> 00:01:23.292
that it's gonna be
about my life

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.834
and how many things
I didn't know

00:01:25.876 --> 00:01:27.626
anyone was paying attention to.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:29.542
I never would have thought
that anyone

00:01:29.584 --> 00:01:32.417
would be able to capture
exactly what was going on

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.959
in such a beautiful, like,
intimate way.

00:01:39.626 --> 00:01:41.584
When we were halfway done
with the movie,

00:01:41.626 --> 00:01:44.667
we just paused it and we called
my mom and dad at home

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:47.459
and we sat there, like,
all of us, we were just like,

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.167
"We love you.
You're such good parents."

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:52.250
It was-- I mean, I know they're
amazing parents,

00:01:52.292 --> 00:01:54.417
it was just so beautiful
to see it.

00:01:54.459 --> 00:01:57.292
I didn't get to really
appreciate how amazing they are

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.334
and always have been,
so I think that's--

00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:01.626
that's the perspective
that changed a little for me.

00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:07.209
We see things for how
we see them,

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.209
and Finneas, as my brother,
was talking about how

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.626
it was really interesting
for him to watch the movie

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:15.250
because he was seeing me
in a different perspective

00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:18.209
than he's even seen before.
Oh, my God. Shut up.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.751
He was telling me that there was
just certain things that are in
the doc

00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:22.542
that he was like,
"That's not ever something

00:02:22.584 --> 00:02:26.209
I've ever thought about, you know,
with you, but it's you."

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:34.042
Um, you know, they were filming
for so long,

00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:35.959
that we got so used
to the cameras

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.334
that I don't remember when
a camera was or wasn't there.

00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:42.334
I don't, like, close up
in front of, like, a camera,

00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:44.667
which is, like, a blessing
and a curse, I think.

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:47.918
There's certain things
in the doc that I never planned
on sharing with the world.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:50.667
There's a lot of stuff
that was very traumatic for me

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:53.042
that is in the doc
that I had to relive watching,

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:54.709
and it's kind of horrible
to think about

00:02:54.751 --> 00:02:57.709
millions of people
having access to it.

00:02:57.751 --> 00:03:00.918
But, it's good.

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:04.542
♪ I don't need a... ♪

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.292
I think it's cool for people
to see another side

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.083
that they didn't know was--
was there the entire time.

00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:14.459
So I have to just hide that,
not just like-- I don't know.

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.125
I don't know. I'm nervous.
I'm very nervous.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:18.834
Scared? I'm very scared.

00:03:18.876 --> 00:03:21.417
- Man: You should be excited.
- Oh, God.

00:03:25.042 --> 00:03:27.542
I'm very excited for the fans
to see this doc.

00:03:27.584 --> 00:03:29.751
I've been, like, jumping
up and down about it.

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:34.000
I'm interested to see how people
react to certain things
in this movie

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:37.918
that nobody knew were going on.
You know, barely my family
even knew.

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:41.792
And know that the fans,
you guys,

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:45.167
you're the only reason I'm,
like, still right here,

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:48.459
so thank you
and I love you

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.584
and I'm so excited
for this journey.

00:03:50.626 --> 00:03:55.000
And I'm excited to be with you
through it all.

00:03:58.292 --> 00:04:00.459
Gotta watch this movie
on a big screen

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:03.292
and turn all the lights off,

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.501
get some blankets,
light a candle.

00:04:05.542 --> 00:04:08.626
You gotta have somebody with you
to, like, squeeze

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:11.334
'cause so many--
so many moments, like--

00:04:11.375 --> 00:04:14.083
yeah, get somebody to squeeze,
get someone to cuddle, like,

00:04:14.125 --> 00:04:17.584
fuzzy blankets,
probably wear pajamas.
That's what we did.

00:04:17.626 --> 00:04:20.876
Candle, lights off, big TV.

